# round 124 (w141): amino acids on deletion-only cell graphs. Records are keyed by deletion gene and merged across datasets, so a Mulleder amino-acid measurement inherits every other screen's added genes: of the 564 amino-acid-scored pinned records, 556 lose ARO4 (YBR249C) and ARO7 (YPR060C) from Cachera's betaxanthin cassette and 499 lose BTS1 (YPL069C) from Ozaydin's carotenogenic plasmid. The Mulleder collection carries none of them, and ARO4 and ARO7 are the committed steps to three of the 19 targets. aadel is w135_aactx with --deletion-only-graph, paired by seed against it.
ESS_SOLVE_TABLE=/scratch/projects/torchcell-scratch/data/torchcell/reference_flux/ess_solve_encodings_SM_aa.npz ESS_FBA_CSV=/home/michaelvolk/Documents/projects/torchcell.worktrees/feat/kinetics-equilibrator-datasets/experiments/027-betaxanthin-metabolic/results/fba_ratio_SM_aa.csv ESS_ARM=pooled ESS_HIDDEN=12 ESS_HEADS=4 ESS_LAYERS=1 ESS_PREPROC=1 ESS_EPOCHS=200 ESS_BATCH=32 ESS_POSW=0 ESS_HEAD=mulleder19 ESS_SEED=2700 ESS_TAG=_w141aadel ESS_OUT=w141_aadel_h12l1p1_e200_s2700 ESS_EXTRA='--node-embeddings pathways prot_T5_all --crps --deletion-only-graph'
